      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Puerto del Rey, the Caribbean’s largest marina, anchors in Fajardo’s harbor and hosts thousands of yachts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fajardo%2C_Puerto_Rico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fajardo serves as the main launch point for boats heading to Culebra, Vieques, and the U.S. Virgin Islands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fajardo%2C_Puerto_Rico",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "From Fajardo, visitors can explore nearby coral islands like Icacos, Palomino, and Diablo, all uninhabited.",
